    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP sets its sights on a high-efficiency slate today, anchored by **Josh Naylor** (72.05) and **Trevor Story** (68.66). **Josh Naylor** is our top play, capitalizing on a soft matchup against Springs; the SP\u2019s 4.84 xERA and favorable park factors provide a massive 19% boost to his base projection. Simultaneously, **Trevor Story** remains a high-floor start despite a challenging opponent, as his 63% SB success rate against a slower delivery allows him to overcome the elite arm of Lugo. We are also leaning heavily into **Vinnie Pasquantino** (67.51) and **James Wood** (67.20); **Vinnie Pasquantino** draws a +14% platoon edge against Gray, while **James Wood** is locked in as a leadoff dynamo with an elite 0.415 xwOBA, turning the 4.16 xERA of Kikuchi into a prime scoring opportunity.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision landed on **Austin Riley**, whose 56.13 score kept him firmly on the bench behind the surging **Max Muncy** (58.20). While **Austin Riley** boasted an elite BvP history (+8%) and strong pedigree, the defensive efficiency of the opposing catcher and a lower-than-ideal batting order position pushed him just below the threshold required to displace our current starters. We are monitoring **Zach McKinstry** (40.93) closely; he sits at the absolute floor of our starting criteria. While he provides necessary positional flexibility, his matchup against Adams is a high-risk venture given the negative SP skill profile and unfavorable platoon split. **Brice Turang** and **Corbin Carroll** remain critical to our strategy, with the latter specifically highlighted for his ability to exploit the slow delivery of Gore, keeping our stolen base upside high even in a matchup that requires tactical precision.",
